59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Considering the risks of social isolation from Option A and the maintenance burden of Option C, Option B seems the most stable. It addresses the unfairness of the current status quo without creating new administrative nightmares.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with @Asuka! Option B is fair and keeps things friendly. While @Ryuji is worried about the rain, I think giving everyone a fair chance is the best way to make people smile.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is just a shuffle of the same problems. It doesn't stop the shoving matches or the rain. Option C actually changes the usage pattern, which is the only way to fix the physical congestion.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, Option C is a fantasy. We have no money for the racks, and @Toshio already told us they're a maintenance nightmare. Option A is the only one that actually generates the funds we need to fix the building.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, generating funds is useless if the process of collecting them breaks the treasurer. Option A is a management trap. Option C is a physical burden. Option B is the only one that doesn't create a new job.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, generating funds is a poor trade-off if it alienates residents, as seen in the neighboring block. @Ryuji, while Option C addresses congestion, the maintenance and cost make it unrealistic. Option B is the most sustainable compromise.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with @Asuka! Even if it's not perfect for the rain, it's the only way to make sure no one feels cheated. Let's choose the option that keeps us all as friends!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If we prioritize ""friendliness"" over the fact that people are actually struggling to get their bikes out, we're just ignoring the problem. Option B is a band-aid. Option C is the only real solution to the congestion.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, you're prioritizing a ""solution"" that we literally cannot afford and cannot maintain. It's not a solution if it's impossible. Option A is the only rational choice that acknowledges the value of the space.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, your ""rational"" choice ignores the reality of the workload. We cannot trade a parking problem for a treasurer's burnout. Option B is the only choice that is actually sustainable for the people running this building.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I understand your frustration, but a solution that is physically or financially impossible is not a solution. Option B is the only path that balances fairness with our actual capacity to manage it.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I really think Option B is the best! It's the only one that doesn't risk making people fight over money or feel stressed about maintenance. Let's just be fair to everyone and keep the peace!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I cannot support Option B. It is a superficial fix that ignores the daily friction and damage I witnessed. If we refuse to address the physical layout, we are simply choosing to ignore the residents' actual struggles.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, your stubbornness is almost impressive. You'd rather have a ""real"" solution that doesn't exist than a ""superficial"" one that actually works. I'll stick with Option A; it's the only one with a brain.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, your ""brain"" ignores the human cost. @Ryuji, your ""real"" solution is a maintenance trap. Option B is the only one that doesn't create a new, unsustainable job for someone else. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,It is clear that Option B is the only viable compromise. It resolves the long-term unfairness without the financial risks of A or the physical burdens of C. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm voting for Option B too! It's the fairest way to make sure everyone gets a turn and we can all keep getting along. I hope everyone can be happy with this!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I cannot in good conscience vote for a system that ignores the physical chaos. Since the others refuse to address the congestion, I vote for Option C. It is the only choice that actually solves the problem.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, your idealism is exhausting. You're voting for a fantasy we can't afford. I'll stick to my guns; Option A is the only one that treats this like a real asset. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
